   "payload": {
    "report_excerpt": "I now have enough verified data. Here is my summary:\n\n---\n\n## Top 5 Domain Availability APIs\n\n### 1. **GoDaddy Domains API (v3)**\n- **URL:** https://developer.godaddy.com/doc/endpoint/domains (v3 API)\n- **What it offers:** GoDaddy's latest API uses a \"quote-execute\" model. The **Discovery** endpoint group lets you check domain availability and get suggestions for keyword queries. You can check if specific domains are available, get registration quotes, and execute registrations \u2014 all via REST API. Requires an API key (free tier available).\n- **Status:** \u2705 Verified \u2014 developer portal is live and actively documented.\n\n### 2. **RDAP.org (Registration Data Access Protocol)**\n- **URL:** https://rdap.org/\n- **What it offers:** A free, open, standardized protocol (replacing WHOIS) for querying domain registration data. Query via `https://rdap.org/domain/{domain}`. **HTTP 200 = domain is registered** (check `status` field), **HTTP 404 = domain is available**. No API key needed. Rate limited to 10 requests/10 seconds on the free tier. Supports all gTLDs and ccTLDs via IANA bootstrap.\n- **Status:** \u2705 Verified \u2014 working via curl. `google.com` returns 200 (registered), random domains return 404 (available).\n\n### 3. **WhoisXML API**\n- **URL:** https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/\n- **What it offers:** Comprehensive WHOIS intelligence platform with 28.7B+ historic WHOIS records, 50B+ domains/subdomains tracked, 7,596+ TLDs. Provides domain WHOIS lookups, domain availability checks, and bulk WHOIS data. REST API with JSON/XML responses. Free trial available; paid plans for production use.\n- **Status:** \u2705 Verified \u2014 site is live and actively maintained. Requires API key/subscription for API access.\n\n### 4. **Namecheap API**\n- **URL:** https://www.namecheap.com/support/api/methods/\n- **What it offers:** Namecheap's XML-based API includes `namecheap.domains.check` command for checking domain availability. Also supports domain registration, transfer, and management. Requires an Namecheap acco",
